# Cache policy for the static assets this Worker serves (Cloudflare Workers static assets).
#
# Cloudflare's default for every asset is `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` — correct, and
# needlessly slow for the 5 MB of hashed JavaScript below, every byte of which is immutable by
# construction. The two rules here are the standard split:
#
#   /assets/*  Vite writes content hashes into these names (index-CcjfYenL.js,
#              index-CE67o2ag.css, pdf.worker.min-DEtVeC4l.mjs). A changed file gets a changed
#              name, so the URL can be cached for a year and never revalidated. `immutable`
#              additionally suppresses the revalidation browsers do on a manual reload.
#
#   /*         The security headers only — deliberately **no Cache-Control**. Cloudflare's
#              default for an asset is already `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`, which is
#              exactly right for index.html: it is the one file whose URL does not change between
#              deploys, and it is what names the hashed chunks, so caching it is how a deploy gets
#              pinned to a stale bundle. The ETag round-trip stays — a 304 on an unchanged deploy,
#              the new shell the moment there is one.
#
# ── Why /* carries no Cache-Control, the hard way ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Matching rules **accumulate**; they do not override. `/assets/index-CboRDc_S.js` matches both
# rules, so writing the default out explicitly under /* produced, verified with curl:
#
#     Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable, public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
#
# — one header carrying two contradictory max-ages plus `must-revalidate`, which is undefined
# behaviour that browsers resolve conservatively. The year-long immutable caching this file exists
# to grant was silently cancelled by the line meant to be a harmless restatement of a default.
# Anything added under /* from here must be a header that is *correct to apply to a hashed asset
# too*, because it will be.
#
# `_headers` applies only to static-asset responses. API responses are the Worker's own and are
# unaffected — a 401 from /api/v1/auth is not cacheable and nothing here makes it so.
#
# Note this file is *consumed* by the asset router rather than served: it is not itself reachable
# at /_headers.

# ── The security headers under /* (audit S1) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The bearer token is held in `localStorage` (see stores/authStore.ts), which any injected script
# can read. That is a deliberate, ordinary SPA trade-off, but it makes the *impact* of an XSS
# total — one injected script is full account takeover, including an administrator's. CSP is what
# caps that impact, and it was previously absent along with HSTS and framing protection.
#
# Every directive below is written to be correct for a **hashed static asset too**, because of the
# accumulation rule documented above: anything under /* also lands on /assets/*.
#
#   script-src 'self'      — no inline scripts. Vite emits external modules only, so this needs no
#                            'unsafe-inline' and no nonce plumbing. Notably NOT 'unsafe-eval'; see
#                            the Zod note under "What the browser check found".
#   script-src https://static.cloudflareinsights.com — Cloudflare Web Analytics. **Added 2026-08-02
#                            after the first browser run against production**, which is the only
#                            place it is observable: Cloudflare injects this beacon into every HTML
#                            response at the edge, keyed off the User-Agent, so neither the local
#                            preview Worker nor a plain `curl` ever sees it. `script-src 'self'`
#                            refused it on all 15 screens, and Web Analytics had therefore been
#                            enabled, injected and collecting **nothing** since the CSP shipped on
#                            2026-07-28. This is P1-2's webfont defect a second time — a policy that
#                            is correct locally and wrong in production — and it is the reason
#                            csp-check.mjs may now be pointed at the live domain.
#                            One exact host, no wildcard. The beacon reports to /cdn-cgi/rum, which
#                            is same-origin, so `connect-src 'self'` already covers it and no second
#                            directive is needed. The trust question is narrower than it looks:
#                            Cloudflare already terminates this site's TLS, runs the Worker and
#                            holds D1, so their analytics origin is not a new party. Cloudflare also
#                            emits the tag with an `integrity=sha512-…` and `crossorigin`, so the
#                            bytes are pinned even though CSP does not itself enforce SRI.
#   style-src  'unsafe-inline' — required, and the one relaxation here. Tailwind v4 and the
#                            Framer Motion transforms both write inline `style` attributes; a
#                            nonce cannot cover attribute styles, so removing this would break
#                            every animation and most layout. Style injection is a far weaker
#                            primitive than script injection, which is the one this file is for.
#   style-src  https://fonts.googleapis.com  and
#   font-src   https://fonts.gstatic.com    — the Barlow / Barlow Condensed webfonts the whole
#                            Industry design system is set in. src/index.css line 1 is an
#                            `@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Barlow…')`,
#                            and the stylesheet it pulls then requests the .woff2 files from
#                            fonts.gstatic.com — two origins, so two directives. Added after a
#                            browser run proved the omission (P1-2); see below. Both are exact
#                            hosts, not wildcards.
#   img-src    data: blob: — data: for inline SVG icons, blob: for pdf.js page rendering.
#   worker-src 'self' blob: — pdf.js is loaded with `?url` (see features/admin/utils/extractText.ts),
#                            so its worker is a same-origin /assets/ URL and 'self' is what
#                            actually carries it. `blob:` is kept because pdf.js falls back to a
#                            blob worker when it cannot use the configured URL directly, and that
#                            fallback failing would break the PDF import in the assessment builder
#                            and the knowledge uploader **and nowhere else** — exactly the kind of
#                            narrow break a CSP ships silently. Verified against pdfjs-dist v6.
#   connect-src 'self'     — the API is same-origin by construction since the single-Worker
#                            consolidation, so this needs no allowance for another host.
#   frame-ancestors 'none' — clickjacking. X-Frame-Options repeats it for older browsers that
#                            do not implement frame-ancestors; the two are kept in agreement.
#   form-action / base-uri — close the two redirect-hijack vectors a lone default-src leaves open.
#
# HSTS is asserted here rather than left to Cloudflare's dashboard toggle so that it travels with
# the repository. `includeSubDomains` is safe for careerlinkai.online, which serves nothing on a
# subdomain that is not this Worker. `preload` is deliberately NOT set: submitting to the preload
# list is close to irreversible and should be a decision made once the domain is settled, not a
# side effect of a header file.
#
# Note these apply to **static-asset responses only** — `_headers` is consumed by the asset
# router, and API responses are the Worker's own. That is the correct split for CSP and framing
# (both are document-level, and the document is always an asset here). If HSTS is ever wanted on
# API responses too, it belongs in the Hono app, not in this file.
#
# ── What the browser check found (P1-2, 2026-07-28) ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# This policy was *reasoned* for three weeks and never *run*. `scripts/csp-check.mjs` drives real
# Chrome against the local single-origin preview and reports every violation per screen. First run,
# 15 screens, two findings — both invisible from reading the file:
#
#  1. **The webfonts were blocked on every single page.** `style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'` does
#     not cover the `@import` at src/index.css:1, so Barlow and Barlow Condensed never loaded and
#     the entire app silently rendered in the system sans-serif — the one break that would have
#     been visible from the back of the room at the defense, and the one that never shows up
#     locally because `npm run dev` serves no `_headers`. Fixed by the two exact-host allowances
#     above.
#
#     The better fix is to **self-host the fonts** and drop both allowances: this repo already
#     carries `@fontsource-variable/inter` from the pre-Industry design (installed, never
#     imported), so the pattern is established. Self-hosting would also stop every student's
#     browser announcing itself to Google on page load and remove two DNS+TLS handshakes from
#     first paint on a school connection. Not done here because it changes what ships and P1-2 is
#     a pre-defense fix; tracked as a follow-up rather than assumed.
#
#  2. **Zod 4 probes for eval, is refused, and copes.** Every page also reports one
#     `script-src blocked eval`, from Zod's JIT feature detection — `try { return Function(''), true }
#     catch { return false }` — which exists precisely so a CSP without 'unsafe-eval' pushes it onto
#     its interpreted validator path. Nothing is broken; validation works. **Do not "fix" this by
#     adding 'unsafe-eval'** — it is the single most dangerous relaxation in CSP, this app holds its
#     bearer token in localStorage (see the top of this section), and the cost of the current state
#     is one console line that a library chose to make catchable.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data: https://fonts.gstatic.com; media-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=(), usb=()
